dht5ByJjJEwpNTFU_KhuvKcBUrGDpQ5apbTmQzoKhAMM1Kzrs65CnjGJ8aBYwyyHbAVgk9hiqFS=
SLxBHfx35J4" class=3D"css-sdwaa1" style=3D"color:#286ed0;-webkit-text-decor=
ation:underline;text-decoration:underline">vice president had predicted</a>=
<span>. But the Iraqis seemed not so much afraid of the invaders, even thos=
e in Humvees, as they were curious. The ones I met were intrigued by finall=
y getting a glimmer of a future not defined by the brutality of the Hussein=
 regime. And it was the Americans who had helped bring about that change.</=
span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:=
0 0 15px"><span>But from the beginning, the United States did not understan=
d the country it was storming into. Twenty-three years later, as it pulls t=
he last of its forces out, it probably still does not.</span></p><table bor=
der=3D"0" cellpadding=3D"0" cellspacing=3D"0" style=3D"width:100%"><tbody><=
tr><td style=3D"text-align:center"><img width=3D"500" height=3D"624" style=
