=3D"font-weight:700">One misstep after another</span></p><p style=3D"font:n=
ormal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>The reason =
for the invasion and then occupation always seemed like a moving target.</s=
pan></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0=
 0 15px"><span>The Bush administration had initially justified it with the =
claim, later debunked =E2=80=94 that Iraq was developing chemical weapons.<=
/span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin=
:0 0 15px"><span>But the military officers and policymakers who moved into =
the palaces of Baghdad=E2=80=99s so-called Green Zone had a new set of rati=
onales: It wasn=E2=80=99t that Hussein was a danger to humankind, or a brut=
al dictator. Instead, as President George W. Bush </span><a href=3D"https:/=
/nl.nytimes.com/f/a/25BzhZvVkz4B3TrjzAbeKw~~/AAAAARA~/OIKJGJuEjqlmXcFjlqaGh=
IFR6_O5pD9AWAgnkwX6SLLlneJ1byOKJj5-N0tykAYrSH_6munmwKsfk9d6fXEnBoV06DsyF10V=
1YGrUZJLRH249-w0qzis-L2OoYnfOF6imI5XOjh3IzgG0IqB06G7DLv3iH9D2ue_yiJmCjc0fU5=
SOHnQHTLLMfzpq75_7Rt2-AZSnSFQeK7rnrRFuhc7cJj-ugTrtXNoqGsflgD90LFYCM2VCOF--a=
uP_A6_zWTPN7GaKgjJfh1lbOdQ43zhFjAZJsE4rQ74sCdJONSa4B8pmo7ZyvabHWttFuRA_6mA4=
GW566Abb1FubLnqoxv-8CadB5bQY3Q3UN0MdlconxM~" class=3D"css-sdwaa1" style=3D"=
color:#286ed0;-webkit-text-decoration:underline;text-decoration:underline">=
put it</a><span>, the U.S. and its allies were there =E2=80=9Cto help the I=
raqi people build a lasting democracy in the heart of the Middle East.=E2=
=80=9D</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333=
;margin:0 0 15px"><span>This began the pattern of changing the justificatio=
n for the continued U.S. presence in the country. Along the way, the U.S.-l=
ed coalition made one disastrous misstep after another.</span></p><p style=
=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>S=
oon after the invasion, a fast-growing Sunni insurgency began taking on the=
 American occupiers. The insurgents bombed U.S. checkpoints and military ve=
hicles; they laid ever more sophisticated road bombs.</span></p><p style=3D=
"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>That=
 made U.S. troops more skittish. They fired upon speeding cars near traffic=
 stops, believing they were being targeted, even when the cars were merely =
carrying families trying to get to safety. Some U.S. troops engaged in huma=
